[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=TCP Server with Authentication v1.0\\\\TCP listener on the Crestron||1
  Cmn2=processor. With Security and Authentication off\\(the defaults)||1
  Cmn3=this module matches the built-in SIMPL Windows TCP/IP Server\\symbol:
  Cmn4=||1plain TCP, no login, Enable / TX$ / RX$.\\\\OPTIONAL SECURITY (TLS)\\
  Cmn5=Hold Enable_Security high, or set the Security parameter to On.||1
  Cmn6=The listener\\uses Crestron SecureTCPServer and the processor certificate.
  Cmn7=||1Lab path:\\  ssl self\\Clients must skip certificate verification||1
  Cmn8=(self-signed). Firmware 1.500.0005+.\\If listen fails, Error$ tells||1
  Cmn9=you to enable SSL.\\\\OPTIONAL AUTHENTICATION\\Hold Enable_Authentication||1
  Cmn10=high, or set the Authentication parameter to On.\\After connect||1
  Cmn11=the server sends:\\  220 TCP Server with Authentication ready\\The||1
  Cmn12=client must send, within Auth_Timeout_s:\\  AUTH <username> <password>\\
  Cmn13=Success:\\  230 Authenticated\\Failure (then disconnect):\\  535||1
  Cmn14=Authentication failed\\  535 Authentication timeout\\Credentials:
  Cmn15=||1Username$ / Password$ parameters (defaults "user" / "pass").\\Non-
  Cmn16=empty Username_Override$ / Password_Override$ win at runtime.\\Authentication||1
  Cmn17=without TLS puts the password on the wire; Error$ warns.\\\\DIGITAL||1
  Cmn18=OVERRIDES\\Enable_Security / Enable_Authentication: PUSH (or hold||1
  Cmn19=high) enables the\\feature; RELEASE (low) falls back to the matching||1
  Cmn20=parameter (default Off).\\Main() samples the digital level so a||1
  Cmn21=held 1 works at startup.\\\\TX$ is sent as-is (no extra delimiter).
  Cmn22=||1Client_Index 0 broadcasts to every\\authenticated client; 1..Max_Clients||1
  Cmn23=targets one socket.\\\\Keep TCP_Server_Auth.clz in this folder.||1
  Cmn24=Target series3 and series4.\\\\VERSION HISTORY\\v1.0  2026-08-24||1
  Cmn25=||1RGW\\- Initial public module
[END]
